From b77470e5b12b27011c846fbbaa10d54b10a981a1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Taimoor Ul Islam <tislam@iastate.edu>
Date: Thu, 30 Jul 2026 15:34:55 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 24/53] kaiair: LDP increments 3+4 - urgency-ordered retx pass
 + N(D)-capped retxs for data TBs (SRB exempt)

- Increment 3: with a deadline active, both intra-slice retx loops serve pending retxs
  most-urgent-first (oldest first-tx = least remaining deadline), so per-slot grant/PDCCH
  caps can never starve a near-deadline packet. Stock FIFO path untouched when LDP is off.
- Increment 4: data TBs are allocated with max retxs capped to N(D)-1 via
  ldp_capped_max_retxs() - the in-deadline budget enforced by construction, with the
  abandonment check as backstop. Applied at the ue_cell_grid_allocator data call sites
  ONLY: SRB/RRC traffic keeps the stock retx budget and is exempt from deadline
  abandonment/ordering (deadline-dropping signaling would kill attach on marginal links).
- k2 note: per-HARQ 'prefer small k2' is not a local knob in ocudu - k2 is fixed by the
  cell-level (pdcch,pusch) slot pairing; revisit only if grant latency proves binding.
- 9/9 LDP unit tests pass. HW smoke pending: bench RF degraded to SIB1-undecodable by
  session end (LDP-off discriminator run shows attach failure is environmental, not code).
